## Why This Is Asked

Tests advanced fairness and isolation in a multi-tenant KCNA cluster; demonstrates practical reliability under bursty traffic.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant rate limiting (token bucket, leaky bucket)
- Global throughput vs. per-tenant isolation
- Distributed state store for buckets (Redis, etc.)
- Backpressure mechanisms and producer signaling
- Canary strategy and measurable success criteria

## Code Example

```javascript
// simplified token bucket sketch
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(rate, capacity) {
    this.rate = rate;
    this.capacity = capacity;
    this.tokens = capacity;
    this.lastRefill = Date.now();
  }

  allow(n = 1) {
    this.refill();
    if (this.tokens >= n) {
      this.tokens -= n;
      return true;
    }
    return false;
  }

  refill() {
    const now = Date.now();
    const elapsed = (now - this.lastRefill) / 1000;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.capacity, this.tokens + elapsed * this.rate);
    this.lastRefill = now;
  }
}

// Global limiter wrapping per-tenant buckets
class TenantRateController {
  constructor(tenants, globalRate) {
    this.buckets = new Map();
    this.globalLimiter = new TokenBucket(globalRate, globalRate * 2);
    for (const [id, quota] of tenants) {
      this.buckets.set(id, new TokenBucket(quota.rate, quota.burst));
    }
  }

  tryProcess(tenantId, n = 1) {
    const bucket = this.buckets.get(tenantId);
    if (!bucket || !bucket.allow(n)) return false;
    if (!this.globalLimiter.allow(n)) {
      bucket.tokens += n; // rollback tenant token
      return false;
    }
    return true;
  }
}
```

Why This Is Asked
- Validates per-tenant auditable trails without impacting throughput
- Ensures tamper evidence via signatures and secure storage
- Checks ability to query across tenants with predictable retention

Key Concepts
- Append-only logs, tenant isolation, data integrity, retention strategy
- Tamper detection using MACs or signatures, and secure storage backends
- API design for write/read with minimal surface area and clear semantics

Code Example
```javascript
class AuditLog {
  constructor(storage, signer) {
    this.storage = storage; // per-tenant append-only store
    this.signer = signer;   // cryptographic signing service
  }

  async write(tenant, event) {
    const entry = {
      timestamp: Date.now(),
      tenant,
      event,
      signature: await this.signer.sign(event)
    };
    return await this.storage.append(tenant, entry);
  }

  async query(tenant, since, limit) {
    const entries = await this.storage.read(tenant, since, limit);
    return entries.filter(entry => 
      this.signer.verify(entry.event, entry.signature)
    );
  }
}
```

